                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.20/515</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Liberian Consul General at New York</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Walker</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the Division of Near Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-04"
                            >December 4, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Murray</hi>: I have just received a cable
                    from the Secretary of the Treasury at Monrovia, stating that the Government
                    feels that additional guns are not necessary for the present time.</p>
                <p>Again I want to thank you for your interest and courtesies in this matter.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Walter F. Walker</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
